**
Malware uses DoH to bypass DNS filtering:
1. Malicious binary queries `https://dns.google/resolve?name=evil.com`.
2. Encrypts C2 IP in HTTPS traffic.
Detection via Zeek:
```zeek
event http_request(c: connection, is_orig: bool, req: HTTP::Request) {
    if ("dns.google" in c$http$uri && !is_orig) {
        NOTICE([$note=DNS_Over_HTTPS, $msg="DoH C2 Traffic", $conn=c]);
    }
}
```
Mitigation: **Block known DoH resolvers** via DNS sinkholes.

